;
; Defines one segment of track.
;
; When the player reaches or passes track.position, the game should subsequently tick once each time
; they go another track.tick_distance. Each tick should adjust curvature in the direction indicated by
; track.tick_direction, with is either 0 for -1 or non-0 for +1. These ticks should continue until
; curvature is equal to track.tick_target, at which point the game should move to the next thing in
; the segments list.
;
; My intention is that gameplay might occasionally involve the player being pushed backwards a short bit.
; In that case it's acceptable not to tick backwards, provided there are no spurious forwards ticks.
;

segment.position:			EQU 0
segment.tick_distance:		EQU 2
segment.tick_direction:		EQU 4
segment.tick_target:		EQU 5

segment.size:				EQU 7
